From e9e6dcb6643339ad1422de13abb10c3779ee4aa6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: c4ffein <c4ffein.work@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 6 Jul 2026 17:23:11 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 8/8] Add front/API contract tests, codegen dim inference, D3
 bug fixes, and backend-proxy chat mode
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Integrated from three subagent branches plus one integration follow-up.

- Contract round-trip suite (tests/contract/, vitest.contract.config.js, scripts/test-contract.sh,
  npm run test:contract): the real apiClient against the real Django backend, no mocks — auth shapes
  and exact error codes, projects CRUD with graph deep-equality round-trip, list-omits-graph,
  ownership isolation. 16 tests; kept out of the unit suite so test:unit needs no backend.
- Dimension inference for generated code (KerasGeneratorDimInference.js): PyTorch recurrent
  input_size and Tinygrad Linear/Conv2d/BatchNorm2d in-dims are now derived by walking the graph
  (units/filters/output_dim chains, Input shape, Flatten products when fully known); uninferable
  cases keep a loud "# TODO: could not infer from graph" on the line instead of a plausible guess.
- D3 bug fixes, each with a failing-then-passing test: selectOnNode is now an idempotent add with an
  explicit toggleNodeSelection for the shift-click call site; removeObserver no longer deletes the
  last observer on a miss (splice(-1)); D3LayerComponent.clone returns its result and uses the
  editor's getNodeId; D3GraphValidation.isKerasError no longer throws ReferenceError. Known-broken
  composite/group feature documented but deliberately untouched.
- Chat backend-proxy mode: when the assistant base URL equals the configured NNVP backend URL, the
  client posts to /api/assistant/messages with the signed-in JWT (no Anthropic key in the browser),
  matching the hardened backend's auth; other custom base URLs keep transparent /v1/messages
  semantics. ChatBubble treats a signed-in backend proxy as ready-to-chat.

Verified: lint 0/0, 173 unit tests, build ok, contract 16/16 against the HARDENED backend,
e2e app/a11y/cloud/interactions 22/22.

